(6247397, 923037, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives :his is excellent - one of those images that confound the brain. It doesn''t seem possible yet here it is. The red of the leaves is magnificent as is the texture on the trunks. The overall lighting balance is top notch. I''d need Viveza to get it that optimised! ;-)<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Lovely stuff!</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives :his is excellent - one of those images that confound the brain. It doesn''t seem possible yet here it is. The red of the leaves is magnificent as is the texture on the trunks. The overall lighting balance is top notch. I''d need Viveza to get it that optimised! ;-) Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Lovely stuff!', '2010-12-07 16:46:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6247400, 918888, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Oh, I really, really like this. It pushes all my gas-mask buttons. The coloration, the cloud, the vignette, the tone mapping, the light - all perfectly captured and presented.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Noting at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: I really wish this was mine! I feel embarrassed about my entry. 10 and a fav.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Oh, I really, really like this. It pushes all my gas-mask buttons. The coloration, the cloud, the vignette, the tone mapping, the light - all perfectly captured and presented. Critical stuff: Noting at all. Overall: I really wish this was mine! I feel embarrassed about my entry. 10 and a fav.', '2010-12-07 16:48:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6247402, 921861, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: What a masterpiece. Superb. The bold centred girl, the imposing buildings, the blurring of the hands, the oh-so-important choice of POV, the monochrome treatment. It just doesn''t get much better than this.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: No!<br/> <br/>Overall: Super-beautiful. An all time fav and the second image I''ve looked at it this FS that has made me feel embarrassed about my own entry. 10 and a fav.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: What a masterpiece. Superb. The bold centred girl, the imposing buildings, the blurring of the hands, the oh-so-important choice of POV, the monochrome treatment. It just doesn''t get much better than this. Critical stuff: No! Overall: Super-beautiful. An all time fav and the second image I''ve looked at it this FS that has made me feel embarrassed about my own entry. 10 and a fav.', '2010-12-07 16:51:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6247405, 922335, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Nicely made - the expression on the girl is priceless and your title led me through the image. The tight framing defines your story well.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The blurred dog is a little bothersome but I can see that was out of your control.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very enjoyable.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Nicely made - the expression on the girl is priceless and your title led me through the image. The tight framing defines your story well. Critical stuff: The blurred dog is a little bothersome but I can see that was out of your control. Overall: Very enjoyable.', '2010-12-07 16:54:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6247407, 923134, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: One of the nicest window in window shots I''ve seen. The crispness of the image is superb and the coloration sublime. I really like your aspect ratio too. I also like the horizontal lines you can see in the reflection and the distortion of the reflected building.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: Fabulously well-executed. Great stuff.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: One of the nicest window in window shots I''ve seen. The crispness of the image is superb and the coloration sublime. I really like your aspect ratio too. I also like the horizontal lines you can see in the reflection and the distortion of the reflected building. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: Fabulously well-executed. Great stuff.', '2010-12-07 16:56:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6247413, 918706, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Bold - our very own ink blot!<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I should get it out of the way and say that I don''t like the image. I think it is the toning that bothers me the most - the way the image is stripped of interest... like it has had the life sucked out of it.<br/> <br/>Overall: This feels a little cynical (beyond contrived). I''m afraid I''ve taken against it a little. A least you got a reaction.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Bold - our very own ink blot! Critical stuff: I should get it out of the way and say that I don''t like the image. I think it is the toning that bothers me the most - the way the image is stripped of interest... like it has had the life sucked out of it. Overall: This feels a little cynical (beyond contrived). I''m afraid I''ve taken against it a little. A least you got a reaction.', '2010-12-07 17:00:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6247415, 923142, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I was glad for the title, it helped make sense of the image. I like the blurriness too - it contributes to a sense of us being too close which helps to transport us into the image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m just not sure there is enough in the image to make it truly interesting.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I was glad for the title, it helped make sense of the image. I like the blurriness too - it contributes to a sense of us being too close which helps to transport us into the image. Critical stuff: I''m just not sure there is enough in the image to make it truly interesting.', '2010-12-07 17:02:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6247418, 922104, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Nice, dreamy image benefitting from atmospheric toning. The blurry dog adds much dynamism to the image and I''m a fan of the chopped head.<br/> <br/>Overall: Nicely done.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Nice, dreamy image benefitting from atmospheric toning. The blurry dog adds much dynamism to the image and I''m a fan of the chopped head. Overall: Nicely done.', '2010-12-07 17:04:38.000000', NULL, 1),
