(6248510, 918888, 24642, '<td valign="top">A very clever idea, well executed.</td>', 'A very clever idea, well executed.', '2010-12-08 06:01:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6248512, 921988, 20799, '<td valign="top">I thought he was holding a weapon there and look it''s this tiny bottle with delicate ornaments... nah, doesn''t scare me, sorry :))). Fantastic shot!<br/>But I know what you mean about creating an entry which will "divide the score", or have a double peak in the score breakdown - more 8-10s and 1-4s than 5-7s, or something like that. That would mean nobody is indifferent to your photo. Now that''s a real challenge. Scores like that immediately remind me of posthumous winners (look at them, they have similar number of 1s and 10s :).<br/>But seriously - 4 photos down, is that you General Patton, sir? :)</td>', 'I thought he was holding a weapon there and look it''s this tiny bottle with delicate ornaments... nah, doesn''t scare me, sorry :))). Fantastic shot!But I know what you mean about creating an entry which will "divide the score", or have a double peak in the score breakdown - more 8-10s and 1-4s than 5-7s, or something like that. That would mean nobody is indifferent to your photo. Now that''s a real challenge. Scores like that immediately remind me of posthumous winners (look at them, they have similar number of 1s and 10s :).But seriously - 4 photos down, is that you General Patton, sir? :)', '2010-12-08 06:02:30.000000', NULL, 0),
