(6250596, 922474, 59267, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Aleema:</b></div><hr/><i> I thought it was illegal to take a picture of someone else''s art work and call it your own, but maybe im wrong does anyone know? Any way i thought for sure this was going to get a ribbon, gave it a 9. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>If the artwork is not private owned nor copyrighted, you are Ok. I guess there are some related laws about the requirement of getting "artist release". National Geographic asked me to get an "artist release" from the windmill owner but later changed to "location release" from the (private owned) tulip farm''s owner when I was willing to compete for the first place in <a href="//www.nationalgeographic.com/energizer/winners/2010/3/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this contest</a>. If I was unable to get the release, I would be DQed from that contest before the voting phase started.</td>', 'Originally posted by Aleema: I thought it was illegal to take a picture of someone else''s art work and call it your own, but maybe im wrong does anyone know? Any way i thought for sure this was going to get a ribbon, gave it a 9.   If the artwork is not private owned nor copyrighted, you are Ok. I guess there are some related laws about the requirement of getting "artist release". National Geographic asked me to get an "artist release" from the windmill owner but later changed to "location release" from the (private owned) tulip farm''s owner when I was willing to compete for the first place in this contest. If I was unable to get the release, I would be DQed from that contest before the voting phase started.', '2010-12-10 11:49:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6250610, 923003, 59267, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dmadden:</b></div><hr/><i> Awesome and congrats! Wish I could see the port of voter that issued the 1 :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I will vote yes for the wish, a geographic map for that would be great!</td>', 'Originally posted by dmadden: Awesome and congrats! Wish I could see the port of voter that issued the 1 :)  I will vote yes for the wish, a geographic map for that would be great!', '2010-12-10 12:04:49.000000', NULL, 0),
